  "body": "It's undesirable how currently, every script fetch uses an algorithm from the \"Fetching scripts\" section, except `importScripts`.\n\nAlso unfortunate is that `importScripts` has its own hooks: validate the state, get a fetch result, and postprocess the fetch result, which are pretty duplicative with script fetching's \"set up the request\" and \"process the response\".\n\nIdeally these should be consolidated, probably by introducing a new \"fetch a script for worker importing\" algorithm in the script fetching section.\n\nWhen I do so I should make sure that it still fits the needs of the service worker spec are still met, and give them a nice pull request to update to whatever changes I make.\n",
